# What Vercel may NOT upload.
#
# Both Vercel projects are deployed with `vercel deploy` from the REPO ROOT and let the
# project's own Root Directory (apps/docs for Storybook, apps/home for the website) pick
# the app. That means the CLI walks the whole repo, and it does NOT read .gitignore — so
# without this file the transient agent worktrees under .claude (108k files, 40 GB) are
# walked too and the deployment's file manifest, which travels as ONE request with a
# 10 MB limit, is rejected with "Request body too large. Limit: 10mb".
#
# Keep this list to things that are generated, transient or machine-local. Anything a
# build needs must stay uploadable.

# Agent scratch space and isolation worktrees (.gitignore:62)
.claude
# repo-cleanup audit output (.gitignore:88)
.repo-cleanup
# Editor-local state, including debug-profile Chrome data
.vscode
# Git history — Vercel builds from the uploaded tree, not from git
.git

# Build and cache output; every one of these is regenerated on Vercel
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/storybook-static
**/dist
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
